{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Show me, I pray, Your kavod.</b> There is kavod above kavod, and what Moses attained at the giving of the Torah was seven sefirot; therefore he now asked for what is above them. And the kavod mentioned here is the supreme, great kavod called the diadem of the illuminating specula, YHWH; therefore you find the word deficient of a vav: כבדך. And regarding the word את, one may say that it comes to include wisdom, as our Rabbis, of blessed memory, intended when they expounded (Deuteronomy 6) ״את ה׳ אלהיך תירא״ — to include disciples of the wise; or he means 'Your kavod' concerning the ultimate kavod, and he said 'show me,' for he sought to see with the physical sense of sight." "<b>And one should</b> examine the matter: if it was impossible for a person to see the kavod while he is still in matter, how did he think to attain it? But Moses, great in prophecy, because his matter had already weakened and diminished during the forty days he fasted, thought in himself that his matter would not prevent his attainment of it, but that he would be as one who is not, and that he would now attain what he would attain after separation from matter. And HaShem, blessed be He, answered him: 'a person shall not see Me and live' — that is, a person who is composed of body and soul cannot attain this while he is still in matter, but only after separation, in the manner of what is written (Psalms 73): ״ואחר כבוד תקחני״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:44.896013521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}